{
 "format": 1,
 "kind": "sweepercad-asset",
 "name": "Elliptic-wing fighter",
 "notes": "An elliptical-wing fighter in the 1930s style, 1:40, in twelve sweeps. Each wing is ONE sweep: an airfoil along a straight spine, the scale graph a half ellipse from the root's full chord to zero at the tip (stations bunched towards the tip, where the ellipse turns fastest), turned 6 degrees up for the dihedral. The tailplane is the same trick tip to tip in a single sweep; the fin a quarter ellipse. The fuselage is an oval swept nose to tail with its side silhouette as the scale graph; the canopy a teardrop sweep half buried in it; the radiator a rounded box under the right wing. The spinner and three blades - each a thin airfoil swept outward with twist - make the propeller. Three colour groups.",
 "graph": {
